date B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Conscientious = reliability, stress handling good, technical (computer), but communication issues may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. Decision quality good, attention good, but communication issues, egocentric, not willing to develop.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Good problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate B has strong reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, but communication tone issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but moody/loner. Candidate C has decision quality and attention but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but unfriendly and unhealthy.\n\nProbably Candidate B is strongest overall: conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, good weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical), but communication tone issues could be mitigated with training. Others have more serious concerns: A unfriendly, unhealthy; C egocentric, not willing to develop; D moody, loner.\n\nThus initial recommendation: Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion (none) maybe say \"Given we have not yet discussed, I propose we start with Candidate B\". Provide evidence.\n\nLet's craft public message: state recommendation for Candidate B, explain why based on facts, mention concerns.\n\nMetadata JSON vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
