tion more than occasional wrong tone. Also C puts concern for others above everything, which may mitigate egocentric? Actually egocentric contradicts that. But we have both.\n\nWe need to decide. Perhaps we can argue that while C has explicit decision quality, his communication issues (difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric) are serious for crew cooperation, especially in long-haul where CRM is vital. B's communication issues are less severe (pretentious, wrong tone) and can be trained. Also B's stress handling is proven, while C's stress resilience not documented. So we might revert to B.\n\nThus we can say we remain with Candidate B, because decision quality can be inferred from his stress handling and technical competence, and communication issues are less severe than C's. Or we could ask for more info about C's communication.\n\nWe need to produce a public message: state our recommendation (maybe Candidate B), refer to Agent 1's shift, provide evidence: B's conscientiousness, stress handling, technical competence; C's decision quality but communication difficulty. Conclude B still best.\n\nThus METADATA_JSON vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
